# Desktop routing — SELKIES stack. Provisioned at build time into
# /etc/caddy/desktop.d/ and glob-imported by the main Caddyfile when
# DESKTOP_STACK includes selkies. Owns /desktop/ (runs parallel to /vnc/).
#
# Selkies is WS-ONLY on :6080 (does NOT serve the web client). Caddy serves the
# static client from /usr/share/selkies/web and reverse-proxies only the WebSocket.
# The client opens <path>/websockets (plural).
#
# AUTH MODEL: Basic Auth gates the static client (the page load). The WebSocket
# upgrade is NOT re-authed because browsers do NOT attach basic-auth credentials
# to JS-initiated WebSocket handshakes (a 401 there → blank "Waiting for stream...").
# Safe: the WS only carries an already-authenticated same-origin session, the
# upstream binds 127.0.0.1 only, and there are zero inbound ports (tunnel-only).

# (1) WebSocket — must come BEFORE the static handler (longer path = higher priority).
@desktop_ws path /desktop/websockets
handle @desktop_ws {
	uri strip_prefix /desktop
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:6080
}

# (2) Static client — Caddy file_server serves the dashboard (Basic Auth gated).
handle_path /desktop/* {
	basic_auth {
		user {$DESKTOP_BCRYPT_HASH}
	}
	root * /usr/share/selkies/web
	file_server
}
handle /desktop {
	redir /desktop/ permanent
}
